      "problem": "Find the point of intersection of the parabola\n$(y-9)^{2}=-3x$\nwith the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "When the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-9)^{2} & =-3x \\\\ 81 & =-3x \\\\ x & =-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $x$-axis at $(-27,0).$",
